==English==
{{was wotd|2006|June|26}}

===Etymology===
{{root|en|ine-pro|*yek-}}
From {{uder|en|la|iocularis}}, from {{m|la|ioculus||a little jest}}, diminutive of {{m|la|iocus||a jest}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ˈd͡ʒɒkjʊlə/|a=RP}}
* {{IPA|en|/ˈd͡ʒɑkjəlɚ/|a=US}}
* {{audio|en|en-us-jocular.ogg|a=US}}
* {{audio|en|en-au-jocular.ogg|a=AU}}

===Adjective===
{{en-adj}}

# [[humorous|Humorous]], [[amusing]] or [[joke|joking]].
#: {{ux|en|He was in a '''jocular''' mood all day.}}
#: {{ux|en|All we had was a short and '''jocular''' conversation.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1865|author=w:Horatio Alger|title='[[s:Paul Prescott's Charge|Paul Prescott's Charge]]|chapter=chapter IV|text=From the tone of the speaker, the last words might be understood to be '''jocular'''.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1896|author=w:H. G. Wells|title=s:The Island of Dr. Moreau|chapter=chapter 15|text=Sometimes he would notice it, pat it, call it half-mocking, half-'''jocular''' names, and so make it caper with extraordinary delight.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1910|author=w:Stephen Leacock|title=s:The Awful Fate of Melpomenus Jones|text=Then papa began to get very tired of Jones, and fidgeted and finally said, with '''jocular''' irony, that Jones had better stay all night, they could give him a shake-down.}}

